  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hello VRChat Team,\n\nCurrently, the VRChat camera can be fixed and positioned in the air at the desired angle. This feature is excellent, though controlling it can be challenging. However, the primary issue is the need for a vertical stabilization mode, as many users frequently take portrait-oriented photos. Users currently use various methods to achieve vertical shots, such as using a special asset called VRC Lens or manually rotating the camera, placing it in a corner, and physically moving into the shot.\n\nThe first method's downside is the significant number of parameters required solely for vertical stabilization, which negatively impacts avatar optimization and other players. The second method is limited by the physical space available and angle constraints within the room. Official support for vertical stabilization would address these issues, enhancing both optimization and user convenience.",
